 M02 depart 11, earlier M01 turnaround ended 9, charge 10, ready 11. If we had not charged, M02 could depart after turnaround at 10 (since turnaround ends 9, ready 10, release 9 so earliest 10). But then M02 departure 10, arrival 10? Then reserve violation. So we must charge. So delay is one slot (depart 11 vs would-be 10). Charge wait: the charge block itself is one slot, so energy wise we used one block. This is minimal. So overall feasible.\n\nNow double-check the corridor closure: COR_07 closed slots 9-32, so PATH_03 for M03 is not allowed. PATH_05 is fine. So our plan uses PATH_05.\n\nOne more: The instance has \"expected_incoming_origin_vertiport\" but \"incoming_deadhead\": null for all missions. So no deadhead.\n\nNow the JSON output: Must include all five missions with decisions. So record_id is \"CA12_CORE_024\". For each mission, we need mission_id, uav_id, held, path_id, depart_slot, charge_blocks.\n\nThus:\n\nUAV_01: MISSION_01: held false, path_id \"PATH_02\", depart_slot 6, charge_blocks 1.\nUAV_01: MISSION_02: held false, path_id \"PATH_07\", depart_slot 11, charge_blocks 0.\nUAV_02: MISSION_04: held false, path_id \"PATH_04\", depart_slot 6, charge_blocks 0.\nUAV_02: MISSION_03: held false, path_id \"PATH_05\", depart_slot 9, charge_blocks 0.\nUAV_02: MISSION_05: held false, path_id \"PATH_09\", depart_slot 17, charge_blocks 0.\n\nCheck sequence: For UAV_02, order M04 then M03 then M05. Departure slots: 6, 9, 17. That respects order. After M04 turnaround slot 7, ready slot 8, M03 can depart 9, so ok.\n\nBut is M03 departure 9 allowed given that M04 turnaround ends at 7, so UAV_02 is at VP_05 and available from slot 8. So 9 is fine. Also M03 due 12, arrival 9, good.\n\nNow check energy for M03 with PATH_05: 0.14496. SOC after M04 is 10.519606, after M03 = 10.374646 >2.5, ok.\n\nNow check M05 departure 17 from VP_01: After M03 arrival 9, turnaround slot 10, ready 11, release 17 so depart 17, ok. Energy after M03 turnaround (no charge) SOC 10.374646, then M05 flight 0.44545 -> 9.929196, reserve ok.\n\nSo all good.\n\nNow verify no pad capacity issues: M04 arrival at VP_05 slot 6, uses pad. M01 arrival at VP_05 slot 8, uses pad. Not same slot, ok. M03 departure from VP_05 slot 9, uses pad. No conflict. Also at VP_04: M01 dep 6, M04 dep 6: two pads used, capacity 2, ok. At VP_01: M03 arrival 9, M05 departure 17: different slots, ok. So fine.\n\nNow charge block at VP_05: M01 charge block slot 10 uses charger, capacity 2, ok. M04 no charge.\n\nThus final decisions.\n\nNow output JSON exactly as requested."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":4242,"completion_tokens":6724,"total_tokens":10966,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4224},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":6390},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4224,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":18},"system_fingerprint":"fp_9954b31ca7_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}